            "content": "Chad saves 40% of the money he earns/receives in a year.  This year, he made $600 mowing yards and received $250.00 for his birthday/holidays.  He also made $150.00 by selling some old video games and another $150.00 doing odd jobs.  How much will he save?",
            "role": "user"
          },
          {
            "content": "First, I calculate Chad's total earnings for the year. He made $600 mowing yards, received $250.00 for his birthday/holidays, made $150.00 by selling old video games, and another $150.00 doing odd jobs. Adding these amounts:\n\n$600 + $250 + $150 + $150 = $1,150\n\nNext, I need to find out how much he saves. Since he saves 40% of his total earnings, I calculate 40% of $1,150:\n\n0.40 * $1,150 = $460\n\nSo, Chad will save $460. \n\nFINAL: 460",
            "role": "assistant"
          },
          {
            "content": "Write your own reusable record of this solved task.",
            "role": "user"
          }
