        "target": "Given the problem, I identified the key quantities: Chad's earnings from mowing yards ($600), birthday/holiday money ($250), selling video games ($150), and odd jobs ($150). The unknown was how much Chad would save, knowing he saves 40% of his total earnings.\n\nFirst, I calculated Chad's total earnings by summing these amounts:\n\\[ 600 + 250 + 150 + 150 = 1150 \\]\n\nNext, I determined the amount saved by finding 40% of his total earnings:\n\\[ 0.40 \\times 1150 = 460 \\]\n\nTo verify this, I checked the calculation by ensuring the percentage was correctly applied and the arithmetic was accurate. The result, $460, matched the expected savings based on the given percentage and total earnings.\n\nThe operation I would reuse is calculating a percentage of a total sum, which is a common task in financial and statistical contexts. This operation is useful whenever a portion of a total needs to be determined.\n\nFINAL: 460",
